A script's interface (main.gxi) is checked by check_script_sig, which compares
only `val`s and the existence of an overlapping impl. The same interface on a
module (m.gxi, checked by check_sig) refuses both programs.

typedef/: main.gxi declares `type T = i64` and `trait Show { .. -> i64 }`; the
  script defines `type T = string` and Show returning string.
    graphix --no-cache main.gx  -> "a"          (accepted)
    graphix --no-cache mm.gx    -> signature mismatch in T, expected type T = i64, found type T = string
impl/: main.gxi declares `impl<'a: Show> Show for Array<'a>;`, the script
  implements `impl<'a> Show for Array<'a>`.
    graphix --no-cache main.gx  -> "arr"        (accepted)
    graphix --no-cache mm.gx    -> does not implement the declared impl ..: missing constraint 'a: Show
